{"kind":"artifact","text":"The committed embed is rebuilt from the browser source that carries the remote-link allowlist. Exact clean pushed head 95374ec2b44779fc712de97c0bec4270c94b9fcb on request/repo-remote-link; local and origin identical by commit SHA and tree hash 59b9a2c0, checkout clean. Under planner's dd883da0 and my promise 29b95948. First artifact at this path from this lane.\n\nWHY THIS PATH HAS ITS OWN ARTIFACT. The resident serves this committed directory, not ui/src. A source-only change would leave the running workroom on a bundle with no allowlist while every test over ui/src passed — the artifact at 34def81d would then be true of the source and false of what an operator's browser actually loads. For a change whose whole substance is refusing to put a scheme into an href, that gap is the difference between the protection existing and appearing to exist.\n\nWHAT CHANGED. Both hashed bundles: the JS because repolink.ts and its callers are new, and the CSS because the anchor introduces Tailwind classes the previous build never emitted. index.html re-points at both, and the two superseded assets are removed.\n\nWHAT I VERIFIED, at this exact head, rather than trusting the build. make ui followed by git status: zero entries. The embed is byte-reproduced from the committed source, so what is committed here is what this source produces, and the head SHA is unchanged by the rebuild — had make ui altered anything, the tree would have moved and this artifact would name a commit that no longer describes the build. make ui-check exited 0.\n\nGATES RUN BY ME AT THIS EXACT HEAD, from runs I watched exit. make ui exit 0 with an empty git status; make ui-check exit 0; npm test --prefix ui 95 tests, 95 pass, 0 fail; go test ./... -count=1 exit 0, 34 ok plus 1 no-test-files, 35 packages, zero failures and zero cached; gofmt -l . empty; go build and go vet exit 0 with no output; git diff --check exit 0.","body":{"commit":"95374ec2b44779fc712de97c0bec4270c94b9fcb","path":"internal/service/uidist"}}